  "description": "DiffDock NIM is NVIDIA's packaged MIT DiffDock service for small-molecule blind docking: it accepts protein PDB text and ligand SDF/MOL2/SMILES-style text, samples protein-ligand poses, and returns ranked docked ligand positions with confidence scores. NVIDIA's current DiffDock docs identify release 2.2.0, the /molecular-docking/diffdock/generate endpoint, /v1/health/ready readiness checks, single-GPU execution, cache mounting at /opt/nim/.cache, and tested H100, A100, L40S, A6000, and A10G configurations. This Forge manifest is onboarding-only despite digest-verified regional mirrors because the current worker shell cannot verify the private NVCR upstream digest and no fresh full Forge GPU matrix was run in this cycle. The recorded prior H200/eu-north2 smoke test remains useful evidence, but B200/B300/L40S/RTX6000 should be reprobed before publication. This is a nonclinical computational chemistry and drug-discovery research workflow, not clinical, therapeutic, toxicity, safety, efficacy, or patient-specific guidance.",
